Reaffirming its strong commitment to the sovereignty, unity, territorial integrity and independence of Mali,

Emphasizing that the Malian transitional authorities have the primary responsibility for the provision of stability, security and the protection of civilians throughout the territory of Mali, and reaffirming the need for full respect for Mali’s sovereignty, unity and territorial integrity in the implementation of all Council measures,

Reiterating the centrality of the Agreement on Peace and Reconciliation in Mali emanating from the Algiers process (“the Agreement”) for the achievement of lasting peace and stability in Mali, welcoming continued efforts from the international mediation under the leadership of Algeria, in coordination with the African Union and ECOWAS, urging all Malian signatories to resume dialogue, fully implement the Agreement and avoid any actions that could undermine the ceasefire or jeopardize the peace process, and emphasizing the obligation of all parties to strictly comply with their obligations under international humanitarian law and international human rights law,

